182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (TO EVALUATE A CLASSIFICATION MODEL, WE NEED MORE THAN JUST ACCURACY. ACCURACY GIVES THE OVERALL PERCENTAGE OF CORRECT PREDICTIONS, BUT IT MAY BE MISLEADING IF THE DATA IS IMBALANCED. PRECISION INDICATES HOW MANY OF THE PREDICTED POSITIVES ARE TRULY CORRECT, WHILE RECALL MEASURES HOW MANY REAL POSITIVES ARE SUCCESSFULLY IDENTIFIED. THE F1-SCORE BALANCES PRECISION AND RECALL, MAKING IT USEFUL WHEN BOTH FALSE POSITIVES AND FALSE NEGATIVES ARE IMPORTANT.)
/E (TO EVALUATE A CLASSIFICATION MODEL, WE NEED MORE THAN JUST ACCURACY. ACCURACY GIVES THE OVERALL PERCENTAGE OF CORRECT PREDICTIONS, BUT IT MAY BE MISLEADING IF THE DATA IS IMBALANCED. PRECISION INDICATES HOW MANY OF THE PREDICTED POSITIVES ARE TRULY CORRECT, WHILE RECALL MEASURES HOW MANY REAL POSITIVES ARE SUCCESSFULLY IDENTIFIED. THE F1-SCORE BALANCES PRECISION AND RECALL, MAKING IT USEFUL WHEN BOTH FALSE POSITIVES AND FALSE NEGATIVES ARE IMPORTANT.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
